      "notes": "All claims are well-grounded. Stated claims quote verbatim from policy text. Measurable claims (E16, E28, E21) are appropriately sourced baseline facts, not projections. Projected claims are correctly tiered and qualified. Direction 'worsens' is straightforwardly supported by the stated expansion of coercive instruments (stop and search, mandatory sentences, new offence) \u2014 no false balance concern. The rationale correctly notes partial overlap with existing law, which moderates magnitude to 'moderate' rather than 'major'; this is a defensible, evidence-grounded call. No party-blind issues \u2014 the rationale judges the policy's structural effect on liberty, not Reform UK's motives. No lever leakage \u2014 the verdict explicitly judges liberty costs, not crime-reduction effectiveness. Stop-watch.org is used only for a measurable baseline statistic (E16) that is attributed to Home Office statistics, which is acceptable. The verdict is publication-ready."
